{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790888589,"nonce":"/5vBJPu7HQLQB58gOoWV4h7eo88=","title":"A digest cannot carry an Investigator's summary, so a policy's digest window is a list rather than an account","message":"**What is wrong.** ADR 0053 §4 lists `digest` as an Investigation subject; its Finding becomes the digest's body for windows a policy asked for. `enrichments_subjkind_ck` (`db/migrations/00069_a_conversation_is_a_case.sql:640`) admits no `digest`.\n\n**Where.** Digest rendering; Investigation subject `digest`; `enrichments_subjkind_ck` widened to admit `digest`; an Investigation for a window started ahead of the window's close.\n\n**Scope.** small.\n\n**Done when.** **A digest never waits on an Investigation:** it sends when its window closes, using whatever Finding for that window exists at that moment, and the built-in digest body when none does (running, failed, exhausted or skipped); a Finding that arrives after the send is not posted as a correction; tests pin a digest sent on time with the Investigation still running.\n\n**Blocked by.** `180a525`\n\n**Mode.** AFK — can be implemented and merged without a human decision. Source: ADR 0052/0053/0054 design session, 2026-10-02.","files":null}]}